{
  "id": "parabolas-u3",
  "title": "Unit 3",
  "subtitle": "Love of Neighbor and Stewardship",
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Jesus taught the importance of loving neighbor and administering well the gifts received from God. Through parables, he revealed that true faith is expressed in concrete actions of compassion, generosity, and responsibility toward what is entrusted to us.",
    "keyVerses": [
      {
        "reference": "Luke 10:36-37",
        "text": "Which of these three, do you think, proved to be a neighbor to the man who fell among robbers? He said, 'The one who showed him mercy.' Jesus said to him, 'Go and do likewise.'"
      },
      {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:31-40",
        "text": "When the Son of Man comes in his glory, and all the angels with him, then he will sit on his glorious throne. All the nations will be gathered before him, and he will separate people one from another as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats."
      },
      {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:14-30",
        "text": "For it is as when a man, going into another country, called his own servants, and entrusted his goods to them. To one he gave five talents, to another two, to another one; to each according to his ability."
      }
    ]
  },
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "parabolas-u3-l1",
      "title": "The Good Samaritan",
      "icon": "sun.max.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "Who passed first and did not help?",
          "text": "A ___ went up that road and saw the wounded man.",
          "options": [
            "priest",
            "Levite",
            "scribe",
            "Pharisee"
          ],
          "answer": "priest",
          "reference": "Luke 10:31"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e2",
          "kind": "typeAnswer",
          "prompt": "Type the missing word",
          "text": "The Samaritan sold his ___ to pay for the care.",
          "answer": "donkey",
          "options": [
            "donkey",
            "purse",
            "clothes",
            "property"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 10:34"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e3",
          "kind": "buildVerse",
          "prompt": "Build the verse",
          "text": "Jesus' instruction at the end",
          "tokens": [
            "Go",
            "and do",
            "likewise"
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "Go and wait",
            "Go and preach",
            "Go and judge",
            "Go and announce"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 10:37"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e4",
          "kind": "orderEvents",
          "prompt": "Put the events in order",
          "text": "Sequence of the parable.",
          "tokens": [
            "Man is robbed",
            "Priest passes by",
            "Levite passes by",
            "Samaritan helps"
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 10:30-35"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e5",
          "kind": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match the actions",
          "pairs": [
            {
              "left": "Priest",
              "right": "Passed by"
            },
            {
              "left": "Levite",
              "right": "Did not stop"
            },
            {
              "left": "Samaritan",
              "right": "Helped the wounded"
            },
            {
              "left": "Neighbor",
              "right": "One who acts with love"
            }
          ],
          "reference": "Luke 10:31-37"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e6",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "A Samaritan showed more compassion than the Jewish religious leaders.",
          "isTrue": true,
          "reference": "Luke 10:33-35",
          "explanation": "While the priest and Levite ignored the wounded man, the Samaritan cared for him with oil, wine, and lodging."
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e7",
          "kind": "listen",
          "prompt": "Who was the neighbor?",
          "text": "The Samaritan was the one who acted with mercy.",
          "options": [
            "The Samaritan",
            "The priest",
            "The Levite",
            "The robber"
          ],
          "answer": "The Samaritan",
          "reference": "Luke 10:37"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l1-e8",
          "kind": "speak",
          "prompt": "Read aloud",
          "text": "A neighbor is one who acts with compassion.",
          "reference": "Luke 10:37"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parabolas-u3-l2",
      "title": "The Talents",
      "icon": "moon.stars.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "How much did the first servant receive?",
          "text": "One servant received ___ talents.",
          "options": [
            "five",
            "two",
            "one",
            "ten"
          ],
          "answer": "five",
          "reference": "Matthew 25:15"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e2",
          "kind": "typeAnswer",
          "prompt": "Type the missing word",
          "text": "The faithful servant earned more ___ by trading.",
          "answer": "talents",
          "options": [
            "talents",
            "coins",
            "gold",
            "money"
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 25:16-17"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e3",
          "kind": "buildVerse",
          "prompt": "Build the verse",
          "text": "The master's praise",
          "tokens": [
            "Well done, good",
            "and faithful servant",
            "enter",
            "into the joy of your master"
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "into the house",
            "into the kingdom",
            "into glory",
            "into paradise"
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 25:21"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e4",
          "kind": "orderEvents",
          "prompt": "Put the distributions in order",
          "text": "Sequence of receiving and settling accounts.",
          "tokens": [
            "Master distributes talents",
            "Servants use their gifts",
            "Master returns",
            "Evaluates how they used them"
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 25:14-30"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e5",
          "kind": "matchPairs",
          "prompt": "Match the servants",
          "pairs": [
            {
              "left": "First servant",
              "right": "Five talents"
            },
            {
              "left": "Second servant",
              "right": "Two talents"
            },
            {
              "left": "Third servant",
              "right": "One talent (buried)"
            },
            {
              "left": "Faithful stewardship",
              "right": "Rewarded"
            }
          ],
          "reference": "Matthew 25:14-30"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e6",
          "kind": "trueFalse",
          "prompt": "True or false?",
          "statement": "The servant who buried his talent was praised as faithful.",
          "isTrue": false,
          "reference": "Matthew 25:24-30",
          "explanation": "The servant was called wicked and lazy for not using his talent; he was punished while the faithful were rewarded."
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e7",
          "kind": "listen",
          "prompt": "What did the faithful servant do?",
          "text": "Listen: The faithful servants multiplied their talents.",
          "options": [
            "Multiplied talents",
            "Hid talents",
            "Lost talents",
            "Gave away talents"
          ],
          "answer": "Multiplied talents",
          "reference": "Matthew 25:16-17"
        },
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l2-e8",
          "kind": "speak",
          "prompt": "Read aloud",
          "text": "To the one with much, much will be given; from the one with little, even that will be taken.",
          "reference": "Matthew 25:29"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "parabolas-u3-l3",
      "title": "The Rich Fool",
      "icon": "hands.sparkles.fill",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "parabolas-u3-l3-e1",
          "kind": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "Why was the rich man's harvest so large?",
          "text": "The harvest was so great that his ___ could not hold it.",
